course: dictionary
lesson: 6233
title: Moan: a sound or a complaint
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Moan can be a low sound of pain or sadness, or the low sound the wind makes in a spooky house. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning fits.
explain: In everyday talk, especially in the UK and Australia, moan means to complain in an annoying way about small things. «Stop moaning about your homework!» means «Stop complaining about your homework!» Ryan moans about homework, so he complains about it a lot.
explain: To check, swap in your meaning and read the sentence again. If the sentence is about small annoying things, moan means complain. A moaner or a whinger is someone who complains a lot.
fact: Moan can be a verb (moan, moans, moaned, moaning) or a noun (a moan).
fact: «Moan» means to make a long, low sound because of pain or sadness.
fact: In informal UK and Australian talk, «moan» means to complain in an annoying way about small things.
fact: A «moaner» or a «whinger» is someone who complains a lot.
fact: Friends can be fun and still have faults, like moaning; you don't have to copy their faults.
exercise: «Stop moaning about your homework!» What does moaning mean here? | Quietly singing | Making a long, low sound of pain | *Complaining in an annoying way | Falling asleep
exercise: Lily's mum says, «no whinging». What does whinging mean? | Sleeping | *Moaning and complaining | Singing | Playing outside
exercise: «Ryan moans about homework, so his teacher shows him a story.» Find and copy one word that means complaining. | story | teacher | homework | *moans
test: Which sentence uses moan to mean a low sound of pain or sadness? | The bell rang at three o'clock | *The injured dog gave a long, low moan | Ryan moans about his teacher | Lily's mum has a rule
test: A friend can be fun and still have faults, like moaning. What does moaning mean here? | *Complaining about small things | Laughing loudly | Running fast | Ringing a bell
exam: Ryan moans about homework, so his teacher shows him a story from Sumer, about 4,000 years old. What is the best meaning of moans here? | *Complains in an annoying way about small things | Makes a long, low sound of pain | Sings happily about school | Falls asleep in class
